Why This Is Asked

Tests advanced security design for multi-account data platforms, focusing on breach containment speed, tenant isolation, and precise policy controls.

Key Concepts

- ABAC with tenant tags and cross-account trusts
- KMS key rotation and per-tenant policies
- Lake Formation permissions and PrivateLink isolation
- Event-driven containment (EventBridge/Lambda) and immutable logging (CloudTrail Lake)

Code Example

```json
// Example conditional IAM policy fragment
{
  "Effect": "Deny",
  "Action": "s3:*",
  "Resource": ["arn:aws:s3:::tenant-bucket-*/*"],
  "Condition": {
    "StringNotEquals": {
      "aws:PrincipalTag/TenantID": "${s3:x-amz-meta-tenant-id}"
    }
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design scalable, secure cross-account access with ephemeral credentials, tenant isolation, and proactive breach testing in a real-world multi-account data pipeline.

## Key Concepts

- IAM Roles Anywhere + OIDC for short-lived, tenant-scoped credentials
- Lake Formation per-tenant access controls
- Cross-account trust with least privilege
- CMK rotation and key policy governance
- Automated breach simulations, revocation, comprehensive auditing

